    <node id="FORMULA 1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Formula 1 is a premier international motorsport competition renowned for its high-speed races, advanced automotive technology, and competitive spirit. The sport captivates fans worldwide, offering thrilling experiences through a series of races known as Grands Prix, held in various locations around the globe. Formula 1 is characterized by extreme G-forces, strategic team dynamics, and the teamwork required among drivers and their teams to achieve victory.

As one of the most expensive sports globally, Formula 1 attracts significant financial investment from teams and spectators alike. The costs associated with attending races can be substantial, reflecting the high-profile nature of the events. This competitive nature and the high costs involved have contributed to its status as a beloved motorsport for many.

The popularity of Formula 1 has surged, particularly through media representations such as the Netflix series "Drive to Survive," which has introduced a new generation of fans to the excitement of the sport. Many individuals, including a diverse group of fans, have developed an interest in Formula 1 through discussions with friends and binge-watching the series. This has fostered a sense of community among enthusiasts, who often engage in discussions about the sport, highlighting its cultural significance.

Overall, Formula 1 represents a blend of adrenaline, risk, and strategic racing, making it a significant hobby and passion for many around the world. Its global fanbase continues to grow, driven by the thrilling nature of the races and the engaging narratives presented through various media platforms.</data>
