    <node id="RAW COFFEE BEANS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Raw coffee beans are the unprocessed seeds extracted from coffee cherries. These beans are initially white before undergoing the roasting process, which is essential for developing their flavor and color. The roasting transforms the raw beans into the aromatic coffee that is widely consumed.</data>
      <data key="d2">048269ae298e29136a527a89c01376b0,4839900ee624ba75c86230d9f423e116,df1142ef01391002e59cd0ee0c586953</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8</data>
      <data key="d7">1fd3fa8bb5a2408790042ab9573779ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ROASTING PROCESS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The roasting process is a critical and crucial step in coffee production that transforms raw coffee beans into aromatic, brownish-black beans used in the preparation of coffee. This transformation is essential for developing the flavors and aromas that characterize the final beverage, making the roasting process a vital component in the journey from raw beans to the rich coffee enjoyed by consumers.</data>
      <data key="d2">048269ae298e29136a527a89c01376b0,4839900ee624ba75c86230d9f423e116,df1142ef01391002e59cd0ee0c586953</data>
