    <node id="FLAG CEREMONY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "Flag Ceremony" is a significant and formal event held to honor the independence of Indonesia, typically taking place on August 17 as part of the country's Independence Day celebrations. This ceremony involves the active participation of students, teachers, and staff from the school community, showcasing a collective effort and national pride. 

During the ceremony, students often volunteer to serve as flag bearers, demonstrating their exceptional preparation and performance. The event serves not only as a patriotic display but also as a traditional gathering that highlights teamwork and community involvement. It is organized by the school to celebrate Indonesia's independence, fostering a sense of unity and respect among participants. 

Overall, the Flag Ceremony is an important occasion that reflects the values of patriotism and community spirit, as students, teachers, and staff come together to honor Indonesia's independence.</data>
