      <data key="d8">202.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Fashion Show was a significant event celebrating Indonesian culture and cuisine, intricately linked to the festivities honoring Indonesia's Independence Day. This event not only showcased the rich traditions of the country but also reflected national pride and identity. It served as a platform to highlight Indonesia's cultural heritage through design, emphasizing the theme of Indonesian cuisine. The Fashion Show was part of a broader celebration of Indonesia's Independence, connecting various activities to the nation's history and values. Overall, it played a vital role in commemorating Indonesia's Independence Day, bringing together elements of culture, cuisine, and national pride in a vibrant display.</data>
